title: what is mine
pid: e0554806-28f2-4127-8034-5dedd57efbd6
body: |2-
  'docs/README.org', 'setup.org', 'usage.org', 'FAQ.org'; 'COMMANDS.org' (Emacs),
  'COMMANDS-nvim.org' and 'nvim-client-deviations.org' (Neovim); 'heralds.org';
  'data-model_friendly.org'; 'glossary.org'; 'diff-view.org'; 'forks.org', 'merging.org',
  'override.org', 'telescopes.org', 'sharing-model.org', 'moving-nodes-across-repos.org';
  'vocabulary.org' and 'hyperlinks.org'; and the short essays, 'this-is-awesome.org' and its
  siblings. 'docs/README.org' links only 'this-is-awesome.org': the other essays,
  'vocabulary.org', 'hyperlinks.org', 'FAQ.org' and 'usage.org' are reached only from
  'README-old.org', which nothing links.
  The Neovim client's setup is in 'nvim/README.org', outside 'docs/', and no page in
  'docs/' links it; whether it is mine I have not settled.
